@{
    ViewBag.Title = "ColorFish Open-Source Color Picker for Chrome and Firefox and Desktop.";
}

<div id="content">

    <div id="page-header" class="page-copyfish">
        <div class="row">
            <div class="span12 whitebg">
                <h1>Colorfish user: <span>Welcome!</span></h1>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row">



        <div class="span12">
            <h3 class="headline">
                <span>Getting started with the Colorfish Color Picker</span>
            </h3>
        </div>

        <div class="span12">

            <p>
                Thank you for installing the  <span class="hired">free and open-source Colorfish</span> browser addon.
                <br />    This page appears only once after the installation to give you some hints on <a href="/colorfish/docs">how to best use Colorfish</a>.
            </p>
            <p>Google Chrome: If you can not see the extension icon, you find it in Chrome's <a href="https://ui.vision/blog/show-hide-chrome-extension-icon/">new puzzle piece icon extension menu</a>:</p>
            <p>
                <img src="https://ui.vision/blog/images/posts/chrome-rpa-icon.gif" alt="Chrome's new puzzle piece icon extension menu" class="responsive-img">
            </p>

            <h2>How to use the open-source color picker:</h2>
            <p>
                <iframe width="560" height="315" src="https://www.youtube-nocookie.com/embed/oO2aEWTNCts?rel=0" frameborder="0" allow="autoplay; encrypted-media" allowfullscreen></iframe>
                </br>Video: The free and Open-Source color picker explained in 60 seconds.
            </p>
            <p>
                <span class="hired">For desktop color picking</span> please also <a href="/copyfish#desktop">install the Ui.Vision XModule</a>. It adds the desktop
                screen capture feature to Colorfish. If you only want to pick colors content inside the web browser, this is not required.
            </p>


            <p>
                <span>&#x261b;</span> <span class="hired">Share Colorfish:</span>

                The more people use Colorfish, the better it becomes. Please help make Copyfish better by sharing it on Facebook, Twitter,...

            </p>
            <p>
                For more information we have the <a href="/Colorfish/docs">Colorfish help page</a>.
            </p>


            <h3>
                <span>For developers</span>
            </h3>

            <p>
                Colorfish 🐟 is published under the GPL open-source license. You can
                find its <a href="https://github.com/A9T9/">source code on GitHub</a>.

            </p>




        </div>
    </div>
</div>
